---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import PageBody from "../components/PageBody.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "usage", label: "Usage" },
  { id: "horizontal", label: "Horizontal scrolling" },
  { id: "styling", label: "Custom styling" },
]);
const tags = Array.from({ length: 50 }, (_, index) => `v1.2.0-beta.${50 - index}`);
---
<DocsLayout page="scroll-area">
<PageBody sections={S}>
  <Section {...S.usage}>
    <p>Add <code>.scroll-area</code> to a container with a bounded height or width.
      It applies <code>overflow: auto</code>, a thin scrollbar, and theme-aware colors.
      Wheel, touch, keyboard, and scrollbar dragging remain native. No JavaScript initialization is needed.</p>
    <div class="tags-demo scroll-area p-4" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="tags-title">
      <h2 id="tags-title" class="title-small mt-0 mb-2">Tags</h2>
      <ul class="tag-list">
        {tags.map(tag => <li class="py-2">{tag}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <Code code={`<div class="scroll-area p-4" style="width: 12rem; height: 18rem"
  tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="release-tags-title">
  <h2 id="release-tags-title" class="title-small mt-0">Tags</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>v1.2.0-beta.50</li>
    <li>v1.2.0-beta.49</li>
    <!-- More tags -->
  </ul>
</div>`} />
    <p>Give a generic scroll region <code>tabindex="0"</code> and an accessible name
      so keyboard users can focus and scroll it. Keep padding for child focus rings.
      In a flex or grid layout, add <code>min-h-0</code> or <code>min-w-0</code>
      when the scroll container needs to shrink.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.horizontal}>
    <p>The same class scrolls horizontally when content exceeds the container's width.</p>
    <div class="scroll-area p-2" style="max-width: 24rem" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Release channels">
      <div class="inline-flex gap-3 text-nowrap">
        {['Stable releases', 'Beta releases', 'Nightly builds', 'Archived releases'].map(label => <span class="surface-container p-4">{label}</span>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <Code code={`<div class="scroll-area p-2" style="max-width: 24rem"
  tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Release channels">
  <div class="inline-flex gap-3 text-nowrap">
    <span class="surface-container p-4">Stable releases</span>
    <span class="surface-container p-4">Beta releases</span>
    <span class="surface-container p-4">Nightly builds</span>
    <span class="surface-container p-4">Archived releases</span>
  </div>
</div>`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.styling}>
    <p>Set these properties on the scroll container or an ancestor.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>--scroll-area-thumb-color</code></td><td><code>var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--scroll-area-track-color</code></td><td><code>transparent</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <Code code={`.release-tags {
  --scroll-area-thumb-color: var(--md-sys-color-primary);
  --scroll-area-track-color: var(--md-sys-color-surface-container);
}`} />
    <p>Use colors with enough contrast against the track and container.
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/css-scrollbars-1/">Native scrollbar styling</a>
      follows the browser and operating system, so shape, exact width, and automatic
      hiding can differ. Older WebKit engines use rounded 8px scrollbars.
      Forced-colors mode restores system colors and the default width.</p>
    <p>For a selective Sass build, include <code>"scroll-area"</code> in <code>$utilities</code>.</p>
  </Section>
</PageBody>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .tags-demo {
    width: 12rem;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: 18rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .tag-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .tag-list > li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant); }
</style>
